{"type":"text","timestamp":1794589597763,"sessionID":"ses_e2a2563c6ffeCw8k2ZmSqa4LP7","part":{"id":"prt_1d5e00b28002dOpFQKbcXRWqBQ","sessionID":"ses_e2a2563c6ffeCw8k2ZmSqa4LP7","messageID":"msg_1d5df82bc001jsUIYUlwdqzIxF","type":"text","text":"Task T034 is complete. Here is the report.\n\n## Files written\n\n1. `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`\n   - Added eight cases: seven successful launch shapes (`env node`, `/usr/bin/env node`, `bash -lc`, `zsh -c`, `node --no-warnings`, `&&` stuck to a word, `;` stuck to a word) and one `echo \"x && node …\"` case that must stay unwired.\n2. `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`\n   - Removed `stripQuotes`, `startsCommand`, and the old `runsMarker` body.\n   - Added a quote-aware word reader that honours single quotes, double quotes, backslash escapes, and ends simple commands at `&&`, `||`, `;`, `|` or newline even when stuck to a word.\n   - Added leading-assignment and `env` unwrapping, node-flag skipping, marker-suffix matching, and up-to-two-level `bash`/`sh`/`zsh -c` script re-reading.\n   - Kept the existing “A mention is not a wired hook” comment.\n\n## Verify output\n\nFirst run, before the fix, failed as described:\n\n```\n✖ passes a launch that starts node through env\n✖ passes a launch that starts node through an absolute env\n✖ passes a launch that runs node inside a bash login command\n✖ passes a launch that runs node inside a zsh command\n✖ passes a launch that gives node a flag\n✖ passes a launch whose separator sticks to the previous word\n✖ passes a launch whose semicolon sticks to the previous word\n✖ names a runtime whose entry echoes a quoted command\n```\n\nPost-fix `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`:\n\n```\nℹ tests 16\nℹ pass 16\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n`node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .`:\n\n```\nok claude\nok codex\nok cursor\nok devin\n```\n\n`node specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/planning/probe-hook-shapes.cjs`:\n\n```\nplain node: exit 0 ok claude\nenv node: exit 0 ok claude\n/usr/bin/env node: exit 0 ok claude\nbash -lc: exit 0 ok claude\nzsh -c: exit 0 ok claude\nnode with a flag: exit 0 ok claude\n&& stuck to the word: exit 0 ok claude\n; stuck to the word: exit 0 ok claude\nthe repository shape: exit 0 ok claude\necho with a quoted script: exit 1 hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json\necho of node: exit 1 hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json\nthis repository: exit 0 ok claude, ok codex, ok cursor, ok devin\n```\n\nBoth files pass `node --check`. I did not tick the task checkbox, and no other files were touched. Nothing in the task was left undone.","time":{"start":1794589592360,"end":1794589597763}}}
